m('''## 06. Factor Construction\n\nLet $g^X_t=100[\\log(IP^X_t)-\\log(IP^X_{t-12})]$. The predeclared factor is $F_t=g^{printing}_{t-2}-g^{manufacturing}_{t-2}$ and the target is $Y_t=g^{paper}_{t+3}$. Each Ridge model uses training-only standardization and fixed $\\alpha=10$; no future-mean scaling or optimized exposure weights. Overlapping 12-month growth windows imply serially dependent targets.''')
